.SH NAME
.PP
auto-remove-from-group - Remove a user from a supplemental group

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-remove-from-group user group
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
user    The user to remove from a group
group   The group from which the user is removed
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-remove-from-group
command removes a user from a supplemental group.  It cannot,
of course, remove a user from their primary group.

Note that the user may lose permissions on any files/directories
owned by that group.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

